parser
======

Pyxplot's command-line parser. The grammar of every command is written in
buildScripts/parser_data.dat; at build time, buildScripts/parser_data.py turns
it into cmdList.c and cmdList.h. Each line of input is compiled into a list of
atoms, which are executed to fill a stack of the command's parameters, and the
command is then dispatched to the code which implements it.

cmdList.c, cmdList.h (generated at build time; not in the repository)
    The grammar of every command, in a compact form, and #defines giving the
    stack slot in which each of a command's parameters is stored.

parser.h
    The types used throughout the parser: the nodes of the syntax trees, the
    atoms and lines of compiled commands, and the state of the parser between
    lines of a multi-line command.

parserInit.c
    When Pyxplot starts, reads the grammar in cmdList.c into a tree of syntax
    nodes for each command.

parserCompile.c
    Matches each line of input against the syntax trees, and compiles it into
    atoms. It also handles { } blocks of code and inline data which span
    several lines, macro and `shell command` substitution, the list of what was
    expected in syntax error messages, and tab completion.

parserExecute.c
    Executes compiled lines: evaluates each atom, checks that its value has the
    type required (e.g. a length or an angle), and places it on the command's
    stack of parameters.

parserShell.c
    Dispatches each command, with its stack of parameters, to the function
    which implements it, mostly in commands/ and canvasItems.c. A few short
    commands are implemented here directly.
